## Setup: Databases

This repository expects reference databases to be available under the `data/dbs` tree by default. For portability across platforms, the Docker Compose file mounts paths using the `DB_ROOT`, `RUNS_DIR`, and `CONFIG_DIR` environment variables (see `docker-compose.yml`).

- Copy the example environment file before starting (creates defaults used by Docker Compose):

```
cp .env.example .env
```

- Download reference databases (SILVA and PR2) into the default local location `./data/dbs` using the included helper script:

```
./scripts/setup_databases.sh ./data/dbs
```

The script will skip files that already exist. To download a BOLD fasta, set `BOLD_URL` in the environment or pass it when invoking the script:

```
BOLD_URL="https://example.org/bold.fasta.gz" ./scripts/setup_databases.sh ./data/dbs
```

After populating `./data/dbs`, start the app with Docker Compose:

```
docker compose up --build
```










